+
+### Overload step on fresh samples (2026-10-29)
+
+`Com_ApRetarget` already zeroed `busyN`; the EMA, however, was seeded from one sample and had alpha 1/16, and the
+overload step fired after 24 samples. The EMA now starts as a running mean (alpha 1/(n+1) for the first 16 samples)
+and the overload step needs `AP_OVERLOAD_N` = 90 fresh samples at the current rate (about 0.8 s), so the step target
+is computed from samples taken only at that rate. Thresholds (0.92/0.88/0.80), the 3 s spacing and the deny logic are
+unchanged. The probe revert keeps its 24-sample check.
